{
  "about": "Shared vectors for a window's picture settings per camera (docs/UX.md 'Fill Tiles'): read by apps/macos NVRCoreTests (TileViewsTests.swift) and apps/windows NvrView.Tiles.Tests (TileViewsTests.cs) and NvrView.Shell.Tests. 'pan': TileZoom at 1x on a filled picture: 'zoom' and 'result' are [scale, center x, center y] (fractions of the picture), 'drag' is in tile units (the picture follows), 'zoomTo' zooms around the tile's middle instead, 'visible' is the part of the picture shown [x, y, width, height]. 'fill': operations on an empty window ('window' sets the window's Fill Tiles, 'tile' a camera's own choice, 'zoom' a camera's [scale, x, y]), then each camera's effective fill, the choices kept, whether the switch is mixed, and how many cameras are kept. 'saved': windows.json members of one window, and what is read back: the window's fill and the entries, oldest first, as [device, channel, lens, scale, x, y, fill or null].",
